<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <!-- Phase 787 — the F* models under proofs/, extracted to F# and compiled
         so the differential hosts can RUN them beside production.

         Every file under custard/ is GENERATED (Phase 957): one run of
         Custard's F# backend over the nine models writes the modules, the
         support library `FStarCustard.fs` they all open, and `Custard.fsproj`
         listing them in compile order; `proofs/check.ps1` re-runs that
         extraction and byte-compares every file against the committed copy,
         so editing one by hand is a change the proof leg refuses rather than
         one it absorbs. They are committed nonetheless, and deliberately:
         the F* toolchain is a 230 MB download, and requiring it to BUILD the
         repo would put a prover on the critical path of every contributor
         and every CI job that has nothing to do with proofs. The committed
         extraction is the seam — `VerifyAll` compiles it like any other
         source, and the proofs job is what holds it honest.

         This project compiles the SAME files Custard's own project does, in
         the SAME order, and check.ps1 asserts the two lists agree: the
         generated project is built as generated so a layout the compiler
         refuses fails by name, and this one is what the hosts reference, so
         every extraction reaches them through one oracle assembly. The
         hand-written `Prims` shim that preceded Custard (nine names over
         BigInteger) is gone: `Prims.int` is `bigint` and the operators come
         from the generated support library.

         What remains forced by the extractor: `FS0064` (a type instantiated
         less generally than its annotation) off, in this scope only — the
         extractor annotates every binder and some annotations are narrower
         than the inferred type.

         FS0025 (incomplete match) is an ERROR here, as it is tree-wide
         (Phase 624): `Directory.Build.props` beside this file stops the
         repository-wide walk and states the promotion itself (Phase 1037).
         check.ps1 strips the FS0025 token from the `#nowarn` line Custard
         heads each module with, so a match F* left incomplete fails this
         build by name — and is the MODEL's to complete by a respelling that
         changes no theorem, as the decoder's `item_at` was (Phase 957). -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);64</NoWarn>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- GENERATED — do not edit any of these. The order is Custard's
             (custard/Custard.fsproj): the support library first, then the
             modules in the order check.ps1's list names them. A new model is one line
             here, where Custard's project puts it. -->
        <Compile Include="custard/FStarCustard.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/RemotingDecode.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/DisclosureFold.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ToolGate.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ModelInput.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/TaintFlow.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ElmishRing.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ElmishSub.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ElmishLoop.fs" />
        <Compile Include="custard/ElmishRingArray.fs" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
